## STATE MANAGEMENT

git-steer persists state as JSONL files in ry-ops/git-steer-state on GitHub.

### State Repo Structure
  ry-ops/git-steer-state/
    config.json         — Managed repos list, policies, schedules
    audit.jsonl         — Append-only audit log (one JSON object per line)
    cache.json          — ETag values, last-modified timestamps per endpoint
    sessions/
      <date>.jsonl      — Per-session activity log

### State Class (src/core/state.ts)
  state.isDirty()       — Check if unsaved changes exist
  state.save()          — Commit current state to GitHub (called on shutdown)
  state.get(key)        — Read a state value
  state.set(key, value) — Write (marks dirty)
  state.append(key, obj) — Append to JSONL

  On shutdown: if (this.state?.isDirty()) { await this.state.save(); }
  State auto-saves to GitHub on graceful shutdown.
  Crash without shutdown = potential state loss.

